 	abstract = {Suddenly finding the solution to a problem after a period of impasse often comes with a feeling of insight. This subjective experience is proposed to arise as a consequence of predictive processing and unexpectedly large changes in belief. Here, we test whether Bayesian surprise tracks the strength of perceptual insight, providing a quantitative account of subjective discovery.},
