 	abstract = {While attention is known to prioritize stimuli held temporally in our working memory (WM), it remains poorly understood how different features (and primarily, spatial vs. non-spatial) shape internal attention. Here, we test whether feature-based and spatial involuntary internal attention differentially influence action-oriented WM selection.},
